      "seed": 924759622,
      "version": 72,
      "versionNonce": 1370596122,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1742674625588,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design a distributed web crawler",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design a distributed web crawler",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "6zMBK_IE1604EcT2-Vj7H",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 314.09533339910934,
      "y": 223.2890625,
      "width": 932.76171875,
      "height": 1350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4g",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 522396826,
      "version": 1450,
      "versionNonce": 1853317466,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1742675562652,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Functional requirements:\n\n1. Crawl multiple webpages\n2. Extract text data from the webpages HTML content\n3. Further crawl the URL that exists in the HTML content\n4. Store the content\n\nNon functional requirements:\n\n1. Scale to 10B pages\n2. Fault tolerance -> If crawled partially and machine goes down, restart would be required\n3. Politeness: robots.txt provides some guidelines \n4. Efficiency while crawling\n\nScale:\n\n1. 10B web pages to be crawled\n2. Each web page -> 1 MB\n\n100 GBPS machine:\n\n1 GB -> 1/ 100 s\n1 MB (1 page) -> 1 / 100 * 10^3 s\n10^10 pages -> 10^10 / 10^5 -> 10^5 s\n10^5 / 10^5 -> 1 day\n\nCore entities:\n\n1. Domain\ndomainId\nlastCrawledAt\n\n\n2. URL\nurlId\ndomainId\ns3Link\nupdatedAt: timestamp\n\nInput:\n1. Seed URLs\n\nOutput:\n1. Text content of seed URLs\n2. Text content of URL contained in HTML\n\nData flow:\n1. Push seed URLs into the system\n2. System crawls the URLs and extracts HTML content\n3. HTML content is extracted for text content\n4. Text content is stored in DB\n5. HTML content is extracted for URL\n6. The extracted URLs are processed (recursive)\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Functional requirements:\n\n1. Crawl multiple webpages\n2. Extract text data from the webpages HTML content\n3. Further crawl the URL that exists in the HTML content\n4. Store the content\n\nNon functional requirements:\n\n1. Scale to 10B pages\n2. Fault tolerance -> If crawled partially and machine goes down, restart would be required\n3. Politeness: robots.txt provides some guidelines \n4. Efficiency while crawling\n\nScale:\n\n1. 10B web pages to be crawled\n2. Each web page -> 1 MB\n\n100 GBPS machine:\n\n1 GB -> 1/ 100 s\n1 MB (1 page) -> 1 / 100 * 10^3 s\n10^10 pages -> 10^10 / 10^5 -> 10^5 s\n10^5 / 10^5 -> 1 day\n\nCore entities:\n\n1. Domain\ndomainId\nlastCrawledAt\n\n\n2. URL\nurlId\ndomainId\ns3Link\nupdatedAt: timestamp\n\nInput:\n1. Seed URLs\n\nOutput:\n1. Text content of seed URLs\n2. Text content of URL contained in HTML\n\nData flow:\n1. Push seed URLs into the system\n2. System crawls the URLs and extracts HTML content\n3. HTML content is extracted for text content\n4. Text content is stored in DB\n5. HTML content is extracted for URL\n6. The extracted URLs are processed (recursive)\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
